         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/baa85b72-212b-4abc-9158-d2195f90a467,1794174553038/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C1920%2C1080%29%3B' alt='A group of people holding Portuguese flags stands in front of a building.' width='620' height='349' title='A group of Cristiano Ronaldo fans gathered Saturday to commemorate his retirement from international soccer.'/><p>Soccer fans and members of the Portuguese community from across Toronto gathered on Saturday to pay tribute to the career of soccer star Cristiano Ronaldo. This comes after the Portuguese captain announced his retirement from international soccer after 23 years with the national team. Ronaldo's last-ever goal for the country was scored in Toronto in July. CBC Toronto has more.</p>]]></description>
